## Atmosphere Enhancements

Enabled in `handleViewerReady`:
- `globe.enableLighting` — sun/moon-based terrain shading
- `globe.showGroundAtmosphere` — subtle atmospheric haze on terrain
- `skyAtmosphere.perFragmentAtmosphere` — higher quality edge scattering
- `fog.enabled` with `density: 2.0e-4` — distance-based depth haze

No native volumetric clouds in CesiumJS — the cloud pass-through is a CSS overlay effect.

---

## Adding a New Location

1. Add entry to `locations` array in `globe-locations.json`
2. Set `lat`/`lon` for the pin position
3. Calculate waypoint positions using the approach line geometry (see above)
4. Set `targetView` to the Kit camera mode to enter after fly-in
5. Add i18n keys to all locale files (`labelKey`, `transitionMessageKey`)
6. The pin, flight, and transition are all data-driven — no code changes needed

